--- Finding (fast_fourier_transform): a list literal holding a tensor made by a
--- list's arithmetic (`ys * 2`) beside a plain list (`ys`: a `range`, or a
--- collecting loop's list) is an internal error in both modes when the literal is
--- bound to a variable; handed straight to `log` it runs interpreted and does not
--- build compiled.
---
--- crow run -i and crow run alike (exit 1, nothing printed), for the lines below:
---   fast_fourier_transform-1.co: internal error: the lowered program disagrees with
---   itself — a bug in Crow, not in this program: fast_fourier_transform-1 main:
---   line 32: a list of List(Float) holds an item of type Tensor(Float) (and 1 more)
--- (`CROW_IR_VERIFY=report crow build --ir`: the second complaint is "holds an item
--- of type List(Int)"; the IR is
---   let ys: List(Int) = core.range_to(3)
---   let both: List(List(Float)) = [(tensor(ys) mul 2), move ys]
--- — the literal's items are never brought to one kind.)
--- With `log[[ys * 2, ys]]` in place of the two last lines:
---   crow run -i:  [[0, 2, 4], [0, 1, 2]]
---   crow run:     error[E0308]: mismatched types … the compiled program does not
---                 build — the Rust compiler refused what Crow accepted
--- Expected, in both modes: [[0, 2, 4], [0, 1, 2]].
---
--- The same with floats (`ys = for x in [1.0, 2.0]` / `x`, then `[ys * 2.0, ys]`:
--- "a list of List(Float) holds an item of type Tensor(Float)"), with the items in
--- either order, with the tensor in a local first (`zs = ys * 2`, `[zs, ys]`), and
--- with `[tensor[ys] * 2.0, ys]`. Runs: `[ys, ys]`, `[ys * 2, ys * 1]`, a literal
--- `ys = [0, 1, 2]` (a tensor already), and `[ys * 2]` then `push[both, ys]`.
--- Met as a function returning `[re, im]` pairs (a vectorised FFT): a base case
--- `return [ys, ys]` (ys collected) beside `return [c, c]` (c = cos[ys]) is
--- "fn twice: line 7: returns List(List(Float)) from a body typed
--- Tensor(List(Float), [?, ?])" — a joined kind no value has.
ys = range[3]
both = [ys * 2, ys]
log[both]
